PPU-25d904bc8511c6ef3fde84a4e7e53f72478852b0:
  "All New Item Innocents Modifier":
    Games:
      "Disgaea D2 (Artemis)":
        BLES01939: [ 01.30 ]
    Author: bungholio
    Notes: 0001=Dietician (Add bonus points to an item's HP.);0002=Master (Add bonus points to an item's SP.);0003=Gladiator (Add bonus points to an item's ATK.);0004=Sentry (Add bonus points to an item's DEF.);0005=Tutor (Add bonus points to an item's INT.);0006=Coach (Add bonus points to an item's RES.);0007=Marksman (Add bonus points to an item's HIT.);0008=Physician (Add bonus points to an item's SPD.);000B=Muscleman (Add bonus points to an item's ATK and HP.);000C=Sprinter (Add bonus points to an item's ATK and SPD.);000D=Nerd (Add bonus points to an item's INT and SP.);000E=Hard Worker (Add bonus points to an item's ATK and INT.);000F=Patient (Add bonus points to an item's DEF and RES.);0010=Pugilist (Add bonus points to an item's ATK and HIT.);0011=Sniper (Add bonus points to an item's HIT and SPD.);0015=Alchemist (Inflict Poison status upon attack.);0016=Hypnotist (Inflict Sleep status upon attack.);0017=Witch Doctor (Inflict Paralysis status upon attack.);0018=Amnesiac (Inflict Amnesia status upon attack.);0019=Gangster (Inflict Depraved status upon attack.);001A=Professional (Inflict Criticals upon attack.);0029=Pharmacist (Increase Poison resistance.);002A=Coffee Maker (Increase Sleep resistance.);002B=Medicine Man (Increase Paralysis resistance.);002C=Psychologist (Increase Amnesia resistance.);002D=Social Worker (Increase Depraved resistance.);002E=Firefighter (Increase Fire resistance.);002F=Aeronaut (Increase Wind resistance.);0030=Cryophile (Increase Water resistance.) <---The developers probably meant "Ice" instead of "Water".;003C=Guardian (Gain more ability when equipping armor.);003D=Broker (Obtain more money upon defeating enemies.);003E=Statistician (Obtain more EXP upon defeating enemies.);003F=Manager (Obtain more Mana upon defeating enemies.);0040=Sparring Partner (Increase rate of Weapon Mastery.);0041=Trainer (Increase rate of Skill Mastery.);0083=Item General;0084=Item King;0085=Item God;0086=Item God 2;00C9=Kinder Gardener (Decrease damage by 25%.);00CA=Berry Picker (Raise the chances of a Team Attack to 100%.);00CB=Secret Trainer (Boost stat increase when leveling up by 10%.);00CC=Chalkboard Scraper (Decrease accuravy of enemy attacks on you by 25%.);00CD=High Spiriter (Release the target from ailment upon a normal attack.);00CE=Glutton (Damage from normal attacks converts to recover effect.);00CF=Punisher (Halve the target's HP with a normal attack from behind.);00D0=Sweet Tempter (Recover 50% of your HP at the end of your turn.);00D1=Mana Robber (Increase Mana earned by 10% with a normal attack.);00D2=Cat Burglar (20% chance to steal from defeated enemy. (Except against Senators));00D3=All Digger (Inflict Paralysis status with a normal attack from behind.);00D4=Trash Talker (Inflict Poison status with a normal attack from behind.);00D5=Rubber (Perform two normal attacks in a row.);00D6=Sensationalist (Inflict Depraved status with a normal attack from behind.);00D7=Wuss (Decrease physical attack damage by 40%.);00D8=Town Crier (Increase counter attacks by 5.);00D9=Sun Bather (Inflict Sleep status with a normal attack from behind.);00DA=Joke Slapper (Inflict Amnesia status with a normal attack from behind.);00DB=Motivator (Decrease magic attack damage by 40%.);00DC=Sumo Wrestler (Increase damage of an ally monster by 20%.);00DD=Hand Shaker (Never miss a target.);00DE=Beggar (Decrease stats of adjacent enemy by 20%.);00DF=Partier (Geo Effect and Geo Chain damage will heal instead.);00E0=Mode Changer (Odd-turn physical attacks and even-turn magic attacks will be nullified.);00E1=Eraser (50% chance to deathblow enemies under 25% HP.);00E2=Killer (Deathblow enemies under 25% SP.);00E3=Heart's Shadow (Increase stats by 1% per unit with 0 likeability.);00FA=Dengeki PS Shop (Increase EXP, Mana and HL earned by 1% for every hour played. (Max 99%));00FB=Famitsu Shop (Increase EXP, Mana and HL earned by 50% for first 30 minutes of play.);00FC=Love Love Shop (Temporarily share max likeability with units equipped with the same Innocent.);00FD=Tsun Tsun Shop (Temporarily share minimum likeability with units equipped with the same Innocent.);00FE=Revival! Shop (Revive at the Base Panel when you are defeated.);00FF=Fold Shop (Move around the map regardless of height differences and obstacles.);0100=Energy Shop (Recover 10% of your HP and SP at the end of your turn.)
    Patch Version: 1.2
    Patch:
      - [ load, *Disgaea2D53 ] 
